    "proof": "CRT makes the residue coordinates independent; each coordinate has admissible probability (q-2)/q, so centering and normalization give the identity Gram matrix. Fix an admissible r and distinct primes ell_1,ell_2 outside Q. Because W is invertible modulo both, impose r+kW=0 mod ell_1 and r+kW+2=0 mod ell_2. CRT gives one class of k mod ell_1 ell_2 and therefore infinitely many positive k. For all large representatives both numbers exceed their displayed proper factors and are composite, while retaining every local Q condition.",
